These "ever-ascending"  tones are known as "Shepard tones." An
illusion, similar to Escher's illusion of a constantly rising
staircase, is constructed by using shifts in volume and frequecy of
harmonics.

If you have "Mathematica," there are notebooks which implement these
Shepard tones.

As to them being "extropic," not for me. Curious, yes, for a few
minutes. But certainly not something to listen to.

(But then I'm always skeptical when someone lists their personal
favorites and labels them as "extropian." It's just esthetics and
personal taste, not extropian vs. entropian.)

-Tim

